r all $n$, which other inequality also certifies boundedness?","options":["$|a_n|\\le 10$","$|a_n|\\le 2$","$|a_n|\\le 0$","$|a_n|\\le -5$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b26a5a769c3ee3dbc0587830","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_006_bounded_sequence_003","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"What is the smallest $M$ with $|a_n|\\le M$ for $a_n=3+(-1)^n$?","options":["$4$","$2$","$3$","$1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f89afe39d9841e03d57d7b0f","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_006_bounded_sequence_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which pair of conditions is equivalent to boundedness of a real sequence?","options":["bounded on both sides","bounded above but not necessarily below","monotone in one direction","convergent to a finite limit"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4085250b756c93cce876ef1c","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bounded_sequence_b6dd4438_001_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which statement is the definition of a real sequence $(a_n)_{n=1}^{\\infty}$ being bounded?","options":["There is a real $M\\ge0$ such that $|a_i|\\le M$ for every $i\\ge1$","For every $i\\ge1$ there is a real $M\\ge0$ such that $|a_i|\\le M$","There is a real $M\\ge0$ such that $|a_i|\\le M$ for infinitely many $i$","There is a real $U$ such that $a_i\\le U$ for every $i\\ge1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"58bffe3422a1526d0346d5bc","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bounded_sequence_b6dd4438_010_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For real sequences, how are boundedness and convergence related?","options":["Every convergent sequence is bounded, but a bounded sequence need not converge","Every bounded sequence converges, but a convergent sequence need not be bounded","A sequence is bounded if and only if it converges","Neither property implies the other"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"63a433b145bcf53367084c93","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_bounded_sequence_b6dd4438_011_curated20261027_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which sequence $(a_n)_{n\\ge1}$ is bounded below but not bounded?","options":["$a_n=n$","$a_n=-n$","$a_n=(-1)^n n$","$a_n=(-1)^n$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8308879d04a60574e270c333","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_006_bounded_sequence_005_curated20261027_004","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $a_n=n$ for even $n$ and $a_n=0$ for odd $n$. Which statement is correct?","options":["It is unbounded, but it does not tend to $\\infty$","It is bounded, because infinitely many of its terms equal $0$","It tends to $\\infty$, because it is unbounded","It is neither bounded above nor bounded below"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"030e29d1a22052e101bc8a29","time_limit":35},{"id":"expansion_006_bounded_sequence_008_curated20261027_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"A real sequence $(a_n)$ is bounded. Which additional property guarantees that it converges?","options":["$(a_n)$ is monotone","The even-indexed terms $a_2,a_4,a_6,\\dots$ converge","$a_n\\ge0$ for every $n$","The terms take only finitely many distinct values"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"db5080c063b85bda6d276e9d","time_limit":30}]}}